epresents the number of yellow tulips, and the denominator represents the number of white tulips.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $30$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 6}{4\\times 6}=\\frac{30}{24}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  Mia has $30$ yellow and $24$ white tulips. So, the total number of tulips is \n\n$$\n30+24=54.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-147065/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e44aa33-0aca-5cb2-8c89-6391240beed8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-147065"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-147069/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "7dacc8fe-e1d3-56ef-9658-a0f0d744fd33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-147069/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "c5b2c101-a0e5-501b-8cad-6f51fa2176de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-147069/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "91b22ed9-f39e-5ff0-8a05-9a0915585b78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-147069/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "e2e6d0d2-db10-54e1-9d25-513a56951f82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-147069/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" :answer/id #uuid "09edee87-aaf2-516e-8730-78934f0c2762" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-147069/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "590cf8b1-83ec-501d-b6af-13ff123b704f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-147069/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer-field/choices ["q-147069/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" "q-147069/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" "q-147069/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-147069/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-147069/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-147069" :question/id #uuid "18131c5f-3ae2-5978-9dc3-079e0144c30f" :question/math-academy-id "q-147069" :question/problem "A die was rolled $40$ times, landing on an odd number in $\\frac{5}{8}$ of the rolls. How many times did it come up with an even number?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of rolls in which the die landed on an odd number to the total number of rolls is $\\frac{5}{8}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of rolls resulting in an odd number, and the denominator represents the total number of rolls.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $40$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 5}{8\\times 5}=\\frac{25}{40}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the die landed on an odd number $25$ times.\nSo, the number of times the die landed on an even number is\n\n$$\n40-25=15.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-147069/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5406de3-483e-56c2-b9c6-73de6769552e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-147069"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-147076/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "02e23d35-0f7c-5634-b655-ed36c91321ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-147076/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a