e ratio of yellow cells to the total number of cells is $\\frac{2}{3}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of yellow cells, and the denominator represents the total number of cells.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $24$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $12:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 12}{3\\times 12}=\\frac{24}{36}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are a total of $36$ cells in the table. \nSo, the number of green cells is\n\n$$\n36-24=12.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-147076/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5406de3-483e-56c2-b9c6-73de6769552e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-147076"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-59895"] :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of students who wear glasses to the total number of students is $\\frac{2}{5}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of students who wear glasses, and the denominator represents the total number of students.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $15$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 3}{5\\times 3}=\\frac{6}{15}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $6$ students who wear glasses. \n\nSo the number of students who don't wear glasses is\n\n$$\n15-6=9.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-147213/selection/ed46a7ab66f4e1f0492ab8ee0b3b7d22df7bff44011d5a9f713d6c9393035ddc" :answer/id #uuid "61932a42-0dd0-5993-a40a-c0e0de6be2a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "49" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-147213/selection/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" :answer/id #uuid "7bbdc896-c607-5aaf-ba3b-b0fa1594d673" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-147213/selection/c59421689e9802bbe55dc885ef3b88a565922fc724e5a7225b403918fe48989b" :