nominator by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 7}{7\\times 7}=\\frac{14}{49}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are a total of $49$ buttons in the bag. \nSo, the number of green buttons is\n\n$$\n49-14=35.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-147213/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5406de3-483e-56c2-b9c6-73de6769552e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-147213"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-92849/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "e78f491f-2ad0-5eee-bb48-5b935943fe89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92849/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "1e65cf1c-94ae-5599-95b1-860a443bcaf9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92849/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "f641e7e3-d77c-5301-8fc7-f0c6084b5dfa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92849/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "fed6c063-411e-5e42-b59d-ae00306b0dbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92849/selection/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" :answer/id #uuid "dc72e729-7f85-51f7-a701-27baa463e02d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92849/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3204333-0fc4-5209-8ad4-ad30354f3e1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-92849/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer-field/choices ["q-92849/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-92849/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" "q-92849/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" "q-92849/selection/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" "q-92849/selection/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-92849" :question/id #uuid "23d6df1d-9c8b-5bf7-91a5-28904190b917" :question/math-academy-id "q-92849" :question/problem "A rock band has $48$ songs, $\\frac{1}{4}$ of which are ballads. How many of the band's songs are not ballads?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of ballads to the total number of songs is $\\frac{1}{4}.$ \n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of ballads, and the denominator represents the total number of songs .\n\nWe can make a denominator of $48$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $12:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\times 12}{4\\times 12}=\\frac{12}{48}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the band has $12$ ballads. \n\nSo the number of songs that are not ballads is\n\n$$\n48-12=36.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-92849/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5406de3-483e-56c2-b9c6-73de6769552e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-92849"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
